# Keycloak-demo URL/port configuration — DEV / in-cluster (minikube) environment.
#
# SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for every environment-specific URL and port the demo's
# identity tier uses. Swap this file (urls.qa.env / urls.prod.env) to retarget an
# environment — NO code, NO image rebuild, NO realm-export edit.
#
# Two consumers, both driven by THIS file:
#   1. token-handler + data BFFs — the `app-urls` ConfigMap is generated from the
#      [APP] block below and mounted via envFrom (see overlays/*/kustomization.yaml).
#   2. The Keycloak realm — scripts/reconcile-realm.sh reads the [REALM] block and
#      PATCHes the live realm (IdP SAML endpoints + every client's
#      redirectUris/webOrigins/post-logout/back-channel) via the admin API. This is
#      idempotent and run by up.sh after import, so it fixes BOTH a fresh install
#      and any drift — the realm is data in Postgres that import (IGNORE_EXISTING)
#      never re-applies, so env vars alone can't drive it.
#
# Split-horizon: BROWSER-facing URLs use the external host/port (reached via the
# ingress / port-forward); SERVER-side calls use in-cluster Service DNS.

# ============================ [APP] token-handler/BFF env ====================
# Browser-facing KC issuer (redirects + `iss`); MUST carry :5180 in dev (kc-ext
# Service / ingress port-forward). Server-side JWKS uses the in-cluster Service.
KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=https://auth.geowealth.int:5180/realms/demo-realm
KEYCLOAK_AUTH_SERVER_URL=http://keycloak:8080/realms/demo-realm
# Server-side P1 authz (in-cluster Service), NOT browser-facing.
P1_AUTHZ_URL=http://p1-tomcat:8080
# Browser-facing P1 SLO target the /auth/logout 303 sends the user to.
APP_P1_INITIATE_SLO_URL=http://localhost:8080/saml/idp/initiate-slo.do

# ============================ [REALM] reconcile-realm.sh =====================
# Admin API base (browser-reachable KC) + realm.
KC_ADMIN_BASE=https://auth.geowealth.int:5180
KC_REALM=demo-realm
# Browser-facing P1 base → IdP singleSignOn/singleLogout (/saml/idp/sso.do|slo.do).
P1_BROWSER_BASE=http://localhost:8080
# In-cluster P1 base → p1-self-client back-channel logout target (KC → P1, server-side).
P1_INCLUSTER_BASE=http://p1-tomcat:8080
# Browser-facing SPA bases → demo-shared-client redirectUris/webOrigins/post-logout.
# Dev keeps the loopback variants alongside the geowealth.int hosts.
SPA_HOSTS=https://billing.geowealth.int:5184 https://trading.geowealth.int:5185 http://localhost:5184 http://localhost:5185 http://127.0.0.1:5184 http://127.0.0.1:5185
# Browser-facing P1 bases that may receive the OIDC callback (p1-self-client) —
# includes the whitelabel *.localhost hosts the cross-host SSO specs exercise.
P1_CALLBACK_HOSTS=http://localhost:8080 http://c1wealth.localhost:8080 http://john.localhost:8080 http://green.localhost:8080
# In-cluster token-handler back-channel logout URL (KC → token-handler).
TH_BACKCHANNEL_URL=http://token-handler:8080/backchannel-logout
